  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — Platizio NextGen\n\n**Top-level finding: there is no test infrastructure in this repo at all.** `package.json` has no test script and no test framework (no Jest/Vitest/RTL in `devDependencies`), and there isn't a single `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*` file anywhere. Current coverage is **0%**. Everything below is therefore a gap; I've ranked by risk and given skeletons using Vitest + React Testing Library, the standard pairing for the App Router — but per `AGENTS.md`, verify the RSC/testing story against `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before wiring it up, since this Next 16 build may differ from what Vitest/RTL docs assume for Server Components.\n\n### 0. Missing test infrastructure\n**Gap:** No `vitest.config.ts`, no `test` script, no `@testing-library/react`. Nothing prevents a broken build from merging.\n```jsonc\n// package.json — suggested addition\n\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"vitest run\", \"test:watch\": \"vitest\" },\n\"devDependencies\": { \"vitest\": \"^2\", \"@testing-library/react\": \"^16\", \"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"^6\", \"jsdom\": \"^25\" }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. `src/lib/content-types.ts` — pure functions, zero coverage\n`anchorId`, `buildToc`, `readingMinutes` are the highest-value target: pure, deterministic, and feed both SEO anchors and reading-time UI.\n\n**Untested behavior / edge cases:**\n- `anchorId`: unicode/emoji input, empty string, string that's all punctuation (→ empty id), the 60-char truncation boundary, collision when two `h2`s produce the same slug (RichText uses array index as `key`, not the anchor id, but ToC links would collide).\n- `buildToc`: no `h2` blocks → empty array; blocks with duplicate heading text.\n- `readingMinutes`: empty `blocks` array (division by zero risk — `Math.max(1, ...)` guards it, but untested), `table` block word counting, mixed block kinds in one document.\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/content-types.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { anchorId, buildToc, readingMinutes } from \"./content-types\";\nimport type { RichBlock } from \"./content-types\";\n\ndescribe(\"anchorId\", () => {\n  it(\"slugifies basic text\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"What is an AIF?\")).toBe(\"what-is-an-aif\");\n  });\n  it(\"strips punctuation-only input to empty string\", () => {\n    expect(anchorId(\"???\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n  it(\"truncates to 60 chars\", () => {\n    const long = \"a \".repeat(50);\n    expect(anchorId(long).length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(60);\n  });\n  it(\"handles unicode without throwing\", () => {\n    expect(() => anchorId(\"₹50 lakh — क्या?\")).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"buildToc\", () => {\n  it(\"returns empty array when no h2 blocks exist\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [{ kind: \"p\", text: \"hello\" }];\n    expect(buildToc(blocks)).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"extracts only h2, ignoring h3/p/etc\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Section One\" },\n      { kind: \"h3\", text: \"Subsection\" },\n      { kind: \"p\", text: \"text\" },\n    ];\n    expect(buildToc(blocks)).toEqual([{ id: \"section-one\", text: \"Section One\" }]);\n  });\n  it(\"produces duplicate ids for duplicate headings (documents current behavior)\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Overview\" },\n      { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Overview\" },\n    ];\n    const toc = buildToc(blocks);\n    expect(toc[0].id).toBe(toc[1].id); // flags a real anchor-collision risk\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"readingMinutes\", () => {\n  it(\"returns at least 1 minute for empty content\", () => {\n    expect(readingMinutes([])).toBe(1);\n  });\n  it(\"counts words inside table rows\", () => {\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [\n      { kind: \"table\", columns: [\"A\"], rows: [[\"one two three four five\"]] },\n    ];\n    expect(readingMinutes(blocks)).toBe(1);\n  });\n  it(\"scales roughly with word count at 200wpm\", () => {\n    const words = Array(400).fill(\"word\").join(\" \");\n    const blocks: RichBlock[] = [{ kind: \"p\", text: words }];\n    expect(readingMinutes(blocks)).toBe(2);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `src/lib/articles.ts` — registry + data-integrity gaps\n**Untested:** `getArticle` returning `undefined` for an unknown slug, `getArticleBody` returning `[]` fallback (masks a missing body silently — this is a **missing error-handling test**: if an article is added to `ARTICLES` but its body import is forgotten, the page renders empty content with no error), `ARTICLES_SORTED` ordering, and — most importantly — **cross-file integrity**: every slug in `ARTICLES` must have a matching key in `ARTICLE_BODIES`, and `CATEGORY_GLYPH` must cover every `ArticleCategory` used.\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/articles.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ARTICLES, ARTICLES_SORTED, CATEGORY_GLYPH, getArticle, getArticleBody } from \"./articles\";\nimport { ARTICLE_BODIES } from \"@/content/articles\";\nimport { PRODUCT_GLYPHS } from \"@/lib/productGlyphs\";\n\ndescribe(\"getArticle\", () => {\n  it(\"returns undefined for unknown slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"does-not-exist\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n  it(\"returns the matching article for a known slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticle(\"market-outlook-2025\")?.title).toContain(\"Market Outlook\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getArticleBody\", () => {\n  it(\"falls back to [] instead of throwing for an unknown slug\", () => {\n    expect(getArticleBody(\"nope\")).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"data integrity\", () => {\n  it(\"every ARTICLES slug has a corresponding ARTICLE_BODIES entry\", () => {\n    const missing = ARTICLES.filter((a) => !(a.slug in ARTICLE_BODIES));\n    expect(missing.map((a) => a.slug)).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"every ARTICLE_BODIES key still has a matching ARTICLES entry (no orphans)\", () => {\n    const slugs = new Set(ARTICLES.map((a) => a.slug));\n    const orphans = Object.keys(ARTICLE_BODIES).filter((k) => !slugs.has(k));\n    expect(orphans).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"CATEGORY_GLYPH maps to a real PRODUCT_GLYPHS key for every category in use\", () => {\n    for (const glyphKey of Object.values(CATEGORY_GLYPH)) {\n      expect(PRODUCT_GLYPHS[glyphKey]).toBeDefined();\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"ARTICLES_SORTED\", () => {\n  it(\"is sorted newest-first by iso date\", () => {\n    const isos = ARTICLES_SORTED.map((a) => a.iso);\n    const sorted = [...isos].sort().reverse();\n    expect(isos).toEqual(sorted);\n  });\n  it(\"does not mutate the original ARTICLES array\", () => {\n    expect(ARTICLES[0]).toEqual(ARTICLES[0]); // ARTICLES_SORTED must not reorder ARTICLES in place\n    expect(ARTICLES.map((a) => a.slug)).not.toEqual(ARTICLES_SORTED.map((a) => a.slug) /* only if source order differs */);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. `src/lib/legal.ts` — untested lookup + missing-doc handling\n```ts\n// src/lib/legal.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { getLegalDoc, LEGAL_DOCS } from \"./legal\";\n\ndescribe(\"getLegalDoc\", () => {\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown id (no throw)\", () => {\n    expect(getLegalDoc(\"nonexistent\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n  it(\"returns the doc for each registered id\", () => {\n    for (const id of Object.keys(LEGAL_DOCS)) {\n      expect(getLegalDoc(id)?.id).toBe(id);\n    }\n  });\n  it(\"every doc has non-empty blocks (catches an accidentally emptied legal doc)\", () => {\n    for (const doc of Object.values(LEGAL_DOCS)) {\n      expect(doc.blocks.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. `src/lib/products.tsx` — registry lookup\n**Untested:** `getProduct` with an invalid slug (note the `slug as ProductSlug` cast means TypeScript won't catch a typo'd slug at the call site — a runtime test is the only safety net here), and that `PRODUCT_MAP` was built correctly from `PRODUCTS` (no duplicate/missing slugs).\n\n```ts\n// src/lib/products.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { PRODUCTS, getProduct, RISK_DISCLAIMER } from \"./products\";\n\ndescribe(\"getProduct\", () => {\n  it(\"returns undefined for an unknown slug instead of throwing\", () => {\n    expect(getProduct(\"not-a-real-product\")).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n  it(\"resolves every declared product slug\", () => {\n    for (const p of PRODUCTS) {\n      expect(getProduct(p.slug)?.slug).toBe(p.slug);\n    }\n  });\n  it(\"has no duplicate slugs (would silently overwrite in PRODUCT_MAP)\", () => {\n    const slugs = PRODUCTS.map((p) => p.slug);\n    expect(new Set(slugs).size).toBe(slugs.length);\n  });\n  it(\"exposes the shared risk disclaimer text\", () => {\n    expect(RISK_DISCLAIMER).toMatch(/market risks/i);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. `src/components/site/RichText.tsx` — rendering + a real edge case\nThe `switch` has **no `default` case**, so an unrecognized `RichBlock.kind` (e.g. a future block type added to the union but not to this switch) silently renders nothing — no error, no dev warning. That's a genuine missing-error-handling gap worth a regression test.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/site/RichText.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport RichText from \"./RichText\";\nimport type { RichBlock } from \"@/lib/content-types\";\n\ndescribe(\"RichText\", () => {\n  it.each<RichBlock>([\n    { kind: \"p\", text: \"paragraph\" },\n    { kind: \"h2\", text: \"Heading Two\" },\n    { kind: \"h3\", text: \"Heading Three\" },\n    { kind: \"ul\", items: [\"a\", \"b\"] },\n    { kind: \"ol\", items: [\"a\", \"b\"] },\n    { kind: \"quote\", text: \"a quote\" },\n    { kind: \"note\", text: \"a note\" },\n    { kind: \"table\", columns: [\"A\"], rows: [[\"1\"]] },\n  ])(\"renders block kind %o without throwing\", (block) => {\n    expect(() => render(<RichText blocks={[block]} />)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"assigns an anchor id to h2 headings for ToC linking\", () => {\n    render(<RichText blocks={[{ kind: \"h2\", text: \"What is an AIF?\" }]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"heading\", { level: 2 })).toHaveAttribute(\"id\", \"what-is-an-aif\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders nothing (no crash, no content) for an unrecognized block kind — documents a silent-failure gap\", () => {\n    const bogus = { kind: \"video\", text: \"x\" } as unknown as RichBlock;\n    const { container } = render(<RichText blocks={[bogus]} />);\n    expect(container.textContent).toBe(\"\"); // currently silent; consider a fallback/console.warn\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders table rows/columns in order\", () => {\n    render(\n      <RichText\n        blocks={[{ kind: \"table\", columns: [\"Category\"], rows: [[\"Equity\"], [\"Debt\"]] }]}\n      />\n    );\n    expect(screen.getAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(3); // header + 2 rows\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. `src/components/pages/InsightsIndex.tsx` — untested client interaction\nThe category filter (`useState` + `.filter`) is the only piece of interactive state logic in the content pages, and it's fully untested. Also worth checking: is `active` category still valid if `CATEGORIES` changes (not really an issue), and that filtering by a category with zero articles renders an empty grid instead of erroring.\n\n```tsx\n// src/components/pages/InsightsIndex.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport userEvent from \"@testing-library/user-event\";\nimport InsightsIndex from \"./InsightsIndex\";\n\ndescribe(\"InsightsIndex category filter\", () => {\n  it(\"shows all articles by default\", () => {\n    render(<InsightsIndex />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"All\", pressed: true })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"filters to only the selected category on click\", async () => {\n    const user = userEvent.setup();\n    render(<InsightsIndex />);\n    await user.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"PMS\" }));\n    const categoryLabels = screen.getAllByText(\"PMS\");\n    expect(categoryLabels.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    expect(screen.queryByText(\"AIF\")).not.toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns to the full list when 'All' is re-selected\", async () => {\n    const user = userEvent.setup();\n    render(<InsightsIndex />);\n    await user.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"SIF\" }));\n    await user.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"All\" }));\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"All\", pressed: true })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Integration gaps — dynamic routes (`insights/[slug]`, `products/[slug]`)\nThese are the only real \"control flow\" in the app (404 handling), and there is no test proving `notFound()` actually fires for a bad slug, nor that `generateStaticParams`/`generateMetadata` produce correct output. This is the biggest **integration test gap** — everything else above is unit-level; this is where routing and content resolution meet.\n\n```ts\n// src/app/insights/[slug]/page.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ notFound: vi.fn(() => { throw new Error(\"NEXT_NOT_FOUND\"); }) }));\n\nimport { generateStaticParams, generateMetadata } from \"./page\";\nimport Page from \"./page\";\nimport { notFound } from \"next/navigation\";\n\ndescribe(\"insights/[slug] route\", () => {\n  it(\"generateStaticParams enumerates every article slug\", () => {\n    const params = generateStaticParams();\n    expect(params).toContainEqual({ slug: \"market-outlook-2025\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"generateMetadata returns {} for an unknown slug instead of throwing\", async () => {\n    const meta = await generateMetadata({ params: Promise.resolve({ slug: \"unknown\" }) });\n    expect(meta).toEqual({});\n  });\n\n  it(\"generateMetadata returns the article's title/description for a known slug\", async () => {\n    const meta = await generateMetadata({ params: Promise.resolve({ slug: \"market-outlook-2025\" }) });\n    expect(meta.title).toMatch(/Market Outlook/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"calls notFound() for an unknown slug\", async () => {\n    await expect(Page({ params: Promise.resolve({ slug: \"unknown\" }) })).rejects.toThrow();\n    expect(notFound).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n});\n```\nSame skeleton applies verbatim to `src/app/products/[slug]/page.tsx` (swap `ARTICLES`/`getArticle`/`getArticleBody` for `PRODUCTS`/`getProduct`).\n\n---\n\n### Priority ranking\n| Priority | Area | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Test infra setup | Nothing else is possible without it |\n| 2 | `articles.ts` / `legal.ts` data-integrity checks | Silent-fallback bugs (empty body/doc) would ship undetected — highest real-world risk given this is a content site |\n| 3 | Dynamic route `notFound()` behavior | Only real control-flow/error-handling path in the app |\n| 4 | `content-types.ts` pure functions | Cheap, high-value, feeds SEO anchors |\n| 5 | `RichText.tsx` per-kind rendering + unknown-kind case | Prevents future block-type additions from silently no-op rendering |\n| 6 | `InsightsIndex` filter interaction | Only client-state logic in the content pages |\n| 7 | `products.tsx` / `productGlyphs.tsx` cross-checks | Lower risk (only 5 fixed products, unlikely to drift) but cheap to add alongside #2 |\n",
